ing data into categories based on type, sensitivity, or usage, supporting management and security policies.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"数据流转\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The movement and handling of data across systems, processes, and stages within the application environment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"数据存储与分布\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The strategy for storing data across various locations or systems, including decisions on redundancy, access, and performance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"业务系统数据库表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Database tables that store information directly tied to business operations, mapped to specific functional areas.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"信息系统代码\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Unique identifiers or codes assigned to information systems for tracking, integration, and referencing purposes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"所在单位\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A field included in database tables indicating the organizational unit responsible for the data.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"更新时间\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A metadata field recording when a record or entry was last modified, ensuring data freshness and traceability.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"功能总设计\"<|>\"功能设计\"<|>\"The functional design phase builds upon the overall functional design by detailing specific views and architectural elements.\"<|>\"design progression, system planning\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"系统总体架构\"<|>\"功能设计\"<|>\"The system’s overall architecture serves as the foundation for all functional design activities.\"<|>\"architectural basis, design dependency\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"功能视图\"<|>\"功能设计\"<|>\"Functional views are explicitly defined during the function design stage.\"<|>\"view definition, design execution\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"数据视图\"<|>\"功能设计\"<|>\"Data views are developed as part of the functional design to reflect how data supports functionality.\"<|>\"data modeling, functional alignment\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"组件视图\"<|>\"功能设计\"<|>\"Component views are created to illustrate how system modules are structured and interac