ization\"<|>\"The cybersecurity management platform is a centralized system that receives and processes audit data and alert information from trusted verification nodes according to specified formats and standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"物理隔离装置\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The physical isolation device is a security component used to isolate networks, ensuring secure communication between zones.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"交换机\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Switches are networking devices mentioned in the context of the control cloud environment, facilitating internal network connections.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"OMS\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"OMS refers to an operational management system, likely related to power system operations, mentioned in the context of network monitoring.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"监测装置\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Monitoring device is a component used for surveillance within the control cloud environment, possibly linked to cybersecurity monitoring.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"西南分部调控云\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Southwest Branch Control Cloud is a geographical or organizational domain referring to the regional control cloud system under the Southwest Branch, where the servers and trusted verification deployment are located.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全II区\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Security Zone II is a designated security area within the control cloud system, likely representing a specific network or operational zone with defined security protocols.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全川区\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Security Chuan District (likely a typo for \"Security Zone III\" or similar) is a region within the control cloud infrastructure, possibly referring to another security segmentation zone.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"调控云域\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Control Cloud Domain is a logical or technical domain encompassing the entire control cloud system, including servers, databases, and verification modules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家密码主管部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"National Cryptography Administration is the regulatory body responsible for setting requirements for cryptographic algorithms in China.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国密SM3算法\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Guomi SM3 algorithm is a cryptographic hash function standardized by China's national cryptography authority, used for integrity verification in trusted computing systems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可信根\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Trusted root is a foundational component in trusted computing, either hardware-based (e.g., a board card with a cryptographic chip) or software-based, used to initiate and verify trust in system components.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可信基准库\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Trusted baseline library stores expected values of programs, configurations, and other assets for comparison during trusted verification.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"软件形式的可信根\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Software-based trusted root uses CPU for cryptographic operations and provides trusted root functionality through software modules, which is the form adopted in this project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统引导程序可信验证\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"System boot program trusted verification ensures integrity of boot files such as kernel and initramfs before system startup.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统程序可信验证\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"System program trusted verification validates the integrity of operating system components like kernel and system files during loading.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应用程序可信验证\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Application trusted verification checks the integrity of executable programs and dynamic libraries before execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"重要配置参数可信验证\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Critical configuration parameter trusted verification ensures the integrity of configuration files and scripts during access or execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"软件版本管理\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Software version management ensures software consistency and source authenticity through digital signatures and certificate verification.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可信审计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Trusted auditing collects and reports trusted verification results, including failures, and ensures data is sent to the management platform even after network restoration.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"自保护功能\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Self-protection capability ensures the trusted software base remains active and cannot be killed or uninstalled by malicious actors.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"虚拟化计算服务器1\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"Virtualized computing server 1 has installed trusted verification software, which includes the trusted verification module responsible for validating system components.\" <|>\"trusted computing implementation, system security\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"虚拟化计算服务器2\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"Virtualized computing server 2 has installed trusted verification software, which enables the trusted verification module to perform integrity checks on system components.\" <|>\"trusted computing implementation, system security\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"虚拟化计算服务器3\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"Virtualized computing server 3 has installed trusted verification software, allowing the trusted verification module to enforce integrity checks during system operation.\" <|>\"trusted computing implementation, system security\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"虚拟化计算服务器4\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"Virtualized computing server 4 has installed trusted verification software, enabling the trusted verification module to monitor and validate system integrity.\" <|>\"trusted computing implementation, system security\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"虚拟化计算服务器5\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"Virtualized computing server 5 has installed trusted verification software, which allows the trusted verification module to perform static and dynamic measurements.\" <|>\"trusted computing implementation, system security\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"虚拟化计算服务器6\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"Virtualized computing server 6 has installed trusted verification software, enabling the trusted verification module to protect against unauthorized modifications.\" <|>\"trusted computing implementation, system security\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<