    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"日志服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Log Service is a component of the control cloud platform that provides standardized application access logging, historical access record retrieval, and system log writing interfaces. It supports unified collection and management of access and system logs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"访问日志管理\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Access Log Management provides access log recording services for various applications in the control cloud, tracking access history of registered or anonymous users and offering backend statistical analysis for usage frequency and access popularity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统日志管理\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"System Log Management offers log collection, storage, querying, and statistical functions for application systems in the control cloud. It gathers logs via the Log Service or log agents, normalizes them into a uniform format, and enables monitoring and analysis of different types of log information.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"实时告警\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Real-time Alerting involves monitoring the operational status of the control cloud platform, assessing alert information, and improving operation and maintenance efficiency to ensure secure and stable platform operation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"告警管理\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Alert Management includes defining alerts, handling alert actions, displaying alerts, and providing alert interfaces. It supports flexible configuration, diverse display methods, and query functions for various alert types.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"基础服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Basic Services include Cloud Monitoring Service, Alert Service, Log Service, Permission Service, and Task Scheduling Service, which collectively support core platform operations such as monitoring, alerting, logging, user access control, and task execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"云监视服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Cloud Monitoring Service allows users to define custom monitoring metrics and visualize real-time and historical performance through a graphical interface.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"告警服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Alert Service provides interfaces for sending alerts, querying alerts, and checking service availability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"权限服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Permission Service offers APIs for creating users, searching users by EmployeeId or login name, modifying passwords, and validating IP addresses.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"任务调度服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Task Scheduling Service enables centralized management of tasks with support for multiple types (e.g., javabean, jar, url, kettle, shell). It provides functionalities including creation, update, deletion, querying, execution, pause/resume, and recovery of tasks.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"公共模型服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Public Model Service includes Organizational Structure Model Service and Power Equipment Container Model Service, both providing data acquisition, count, list, object retrieval, and related services.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"一次模型数据服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Primary Model Data Service encompasses services for power generation, transmission, substation, distribution, and DC equipment models, each offering data retrieval, count, list, and object-based services.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"二次模型服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Secondary Model Service includes Automation Equipment Model Service and Protection Equipment Model Service, covering components like computer devices, network devices, security devices, auxiliary systems, software, station automation equipment, and distribution automation terminals, as well as AC protection, fault recording, fault location, safety automatics, and auxiliary protection devices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"模型统计数据服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Model Statistical Data Service includes Grid Model Statistics, Substation Model Statistics, Sectional Model Statistics, Power Container Data Statistics, Primary Equipment Data Statistics, and Grid Management Statistical Services.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"展示类服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Display Services provide card-based views for organizational structure, power containers, grid, substations, primary equipment, relay protection, monitoring systems, automation devices, public data, measurements, energy, faults, outage plans, and map visualization.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"交互类服务\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Interactive Services include Evaluation Service, Data Export Service, Conditional Search Service, Help Service, Message Notification Service, Product Information Service, and Micro-application Configuration Retrieval Service.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主机可信验证\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Host Trusted Verification implements a secure computing model using cryptography to perform identity recognition, state measurement, and confidential storage, enabling detection of 'self' versus 'non-self' components to enhance cybersecurity immunity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可信验证模块\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Trusted Verification Module consists of Trusted Root, Trusted Software Base, and Trusted Verification Management Module. It performs trusted validation of boot programs, system software, applications, and critical configuration parameters based on the Trusted Root.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可信验证管理中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Trusted Verification Management Center operates on C/S architecture, enabling centralized management of trusted policies, application updates, and audit information viewing. It communicates directly with the Trusted Verification Module and forwards audit alerts and status information to the Cybersecurity Management Platform.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"西南分部安全三区调控云域\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Southwest Division Security Zone III Control Cloud Domain is the deployment location for the Trusted Verification System, hosting 18 instances of Trusted Verification Module software, one hardware instance of the Trusted Verification Management Center, and one software instance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"网络安全管理平台\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Cybersecurity Management Platform receives audi