    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"PMS3.0\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"PMS3.0 is a system used for project management and document verification, specifically designed to handle milestone information, file uploads, and compliance checks across various project stages.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"RPA\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"RPA refers to robotic process automation technology integrated into the system to enable automatic uploading of approved documents to PMS3.0.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"National Grid Headquarters AI Platform\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The National Grid Headquarters AI Platform is an external system integrated with the current platform to support intelligent query and knowledge processing functions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Project Milestone Management Requirements\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project Milestone Management Requirements are guidelines that define the standards and procedures for managing project milestones, including timely documentation and compliance checks.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Design Contract\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Design contract refers to a formal agreement related to design services, requiring proper signing, timing, and content completeness as part of project compliance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Construction Contract\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Construction contract is a legal agreement for construction work, requiring compliance with bidding notices, signing timelines, and full documentation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Service Contract\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Service contract refers to agreements for non-construction services, requiring complete terms, clear responsibilities, and proper execution timing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Supervision Contract\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Supervision contract governs the role and duties of project supervision, requiring timely signing, proper authorization, and clear definition of responsibilities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Initial Design Report\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Initial design report is a document required during the early project phase, containing technical details and budget estimates, subject to review and approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Estimate Book\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Estimate book is a financial document used in project planning, containing detailed cost breakdowns and serving as a basis for budgeting and control.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Final Settlement Report\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Final settlement report is a document summarizing project costs, comparing actual expenditures with initial estimates, and verifying final amounts.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Project Archive\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project archive refers to all official records and documents collected throughout a project’s lifecycle, including contracts, reports, and approvals.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Project Proposal\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project proposal is a preliminary document outlining project objectives, scope, and justification, required for initial review and approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Feasibility Study Report\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Feasibility study report evaluates the technical, economic, and operational viability of a project before formal approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Approval Document\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Approval document refers to any official written consent or authorization issued by an authority, such as a feasibility study approval or project commencement approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Technical Review Opinion\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Technical review opinion is a formal assessment provided by experts on project plans, designs, or reports, indicating compliance or areas needing improvement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Three Measures and One Plan\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Three Measures and One Plan is a safety-related document package required before project commencement, covering technical measures, organizational measures, safety measures, and implementation plans.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Contract Signing Date\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Contract signing date refers to the specific date when a contract is officially signed, which must be within 